ent for women with BRCA1&#x0002f;2 mutations</article-title><source>Cancer J Sci Am</source><year>1999b</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>283</fpage><lpage>292</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer J Sci Am||5|283||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10526669</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grann</surname><given-names>VR</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacobson</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomason</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Hershman</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Heitjan</surname><given-names>DF</given-names></name><name><surname>Neugut</surname><given-names>AI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of prevention strategies on survival and quality adjusted survival of women with BRCA1&#x0002f;2 mutations: an updated decision analysis</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>2002</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>2520</fpage><lpage>2529</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Clin Oncol||20|2520||bib14|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12011131</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grann</surname><given-names>VR</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacobson</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Whang</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Hershman</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Heitjan</surname><given-names>DF</given-names></name><name><surname>Antman</surname><given-names>KH</given-names></name><name><surname>Neugut</surname><given-names>AI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prevention with tamoxifen or other hormones versus prophylactic surgery in BRCA1&#x0002f;2-positive women: a decision analysis</article-title><source>Cancer J Sci Am</source><year>2000</year><volume>6</volume><f